#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124317 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124508 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce5ddb87-f7c0-5bda-8d6e-ac1728dd2f99" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix Given the Number of Non-Pivot Columns"}] :question/id #uuid "e1036a11-ebb3-594d-aba1-be259eb0596d" :question/math-academy-id "e-5419" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $9 \\times 11$ matrix that has $9$ pivot columns, then what is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))?$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $A$. \n\nSince $A$ has $11$ columns and $9$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is \n\n$$\n11-9=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124318 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124509 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection"}] :question/id #uuid "4aa47a89-9f9b-55d8-ba01-a131b20e6c95" :question/math-academy-id "e-5421" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If ![](images/77/77c0dd8d9b925b3310c5470f272b59e2b9d25bb141295741f1748771b6c454c1.svg) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=2$\n\nII. If ![](images/86/86c4f440750b5d7bf45e8c36b6fd9852c2749ac56331b3e0d76a6901acaf5b60.svg) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=0$\n\nIII. If ![](images/22/2295be7f70c3de36b51784b2919af95695f5520abdb2300287a17852b4cbfce3.svg) then $\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124319 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124510 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a0e3b9-931a-52bd-9ed9-b8001c8de67b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Nullity of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/id #uuid "42d77ab8-0670-55bf-8b99-68270c8e5f2e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5422" :question/problem "Given ![](images/82/829e66e040815801f77e92b2afd97531779864935faf7c9dcf1b0485593db856.svg) what is $\\textrm{nullity}(A)?$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{nullity}(A) = \\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Null}(A)) = 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124510 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a0e3b9-931a-52bd-9ed9-b8001c8de67b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Nullity of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b49d403-4d2e-5a55-8cc6-e0b6dafc62fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269489} {:answer/id #uuid "a4655b35-dd10-5c90-a3c5-4588e6f02753" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270735} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e45be1-da88-5563-87d7-4d0f4cadbf17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270912} {:answer/id #uuid "c6d50fde-1a07-5a7f-8e7d-3ddc422e4c77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271020} {:answer/id #uuid "ee683b21-3e01-5536-9583-0f3ac852d6f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9e45be1-da88-5563-87d7-4d0f4cadbf17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270912} :answer-field/id #uuid "25f09d8d-8def-5366-ab11-07b9ebf9fe2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271578}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59f4ef86-ac62-591e-aa5f-05de601f1524" :question/math-academy-id "q-139975" :question/problem "If $W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(W)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(W)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W))$, we reduce $W$ to row echelon form, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 18 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and  $1$\n non-pivot column (the $2$nd). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(W)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W))=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124508 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce5ddb87-f7c0-5bda-8d6e-ac1728dd2f99" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix Given the Number of Non-Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b7137d1-196e-5467-891f-8a544f21aeba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425381} {:answer/id #uuid "53593f8a-84e1-5e46-9090-20482d8e60a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425386} {:answer/id #uuid "942dbaf5-ecc1-59dd-96cd-09e8f4c50159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425392} {:answer/id #uuid "d1b97ca4-654d-53cf-b7f4-3b50efd771a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425396} {:answer/id #uuid "f87f31f4-b42f-5af1-a0e6-59a42452095b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53593f8a-84e1-5e46-9090-20482d8e60a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425386} :answer-field/id #uuid "72b3a9a3-a8e1-52c0-99d6-ec57e4d43b0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b000b980-8b9a-5a4e-a59b-6de7017a3b28" :question/math-academy-id "q-34901" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $7\\times 11$ matrix that has $7$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(A))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $A.$\n\nSince we are told that $A$ has $7$ non-pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124509 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "285ed021-2a5b-563c-9cb6-a55ef00e5f9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317691} {:answer/id #uuid "7e27ee27-ef83-527f-ad6e-6ed1940373d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317995} {:answer/id #uuid "882c9335-98b9-51dd-8014-126aafeeb87b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318026} {:answer/id #uuid "982ad340-ed13-552d-bca5-2129fbb6d423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318085} {:answer/id #uuid "f19ae1c4-9c02-5103-bc45-ec9e3b3e8123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "285ed021-2a5b-563c-9cb6-a55ef00e5f9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317691} :answer-field/id #uuid "49038ece-c8a5-5724-aab1-227760f5017a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318585}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56ebc46d-299b-5fda-a402-a93bacc04806" :question/math-academy-id "q-34973" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$\n\nII. If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=3.$\n\nIII. If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The matrix $A$ has $3$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425407 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124509 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25d9c3ae-c60e-5f23-8b09-bd6f72672565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425382} {:answer/id #uuid "62c579bb-353a-5222-8c49-b704acbe87e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425387} {:answer/id #uuid "8d34d79c-138f-5ab3-9fb5-c6f333384a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425391} {:answer/id #uuid "b08e9ade-c6e5-5b60-ac34-32e78a9a1641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425393} {:answer/id #uuid "bca9b8c9-b194-53fd-be09-17e6ac4e9236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25d9c3ae-c60e-5f23-8b09-bd6f72672565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425382} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7861d69-8891-56f9-b3bb-6cd69873e91d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd86946f-a577-5d18-8f57-7b7435272376" :question/math-academy-id "q-35200" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and no non-pivot column. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0+1+2=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124510 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a0e3b9-931a-52bd-9ed9-b8001c8de67b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Nullity of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b39024-8f98-5edf-93f7-04a64ee7b6c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425380} {:answer/id #uuid "48411ad1-c867-5f45-b8c7-ce3589fd2218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425384} {:answer/id #uuid "69951a24-a52b-5841-8392-9e70e2c63d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425388} {:answer/id #uuid "7ac52ed7-ea31-518a-95fb-dc6ea725ad9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425390} {:answer/id #uuid "d56c921a-e74a-5b91-bee7-d13092469fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48411ad1-c867-5f45-b8c7-ce3589fd2218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425384} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c9771c3-f30b-56b9-83e9-dd0e274a3d9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "83850766-9b1b-5a37-bf38-12d47d12c4d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-35347" :question/problem "Given $G=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -15 & -12 & -16\\end{aligned}],\\,$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(G))?$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(G))$, we reduce $G$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -15 & -12 & -16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -15 & -12 & -16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{9}{2} & \\frac{11}{4} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $4$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(G))=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425405 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124508 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce5ddb87-f7c0-5bda-8d6e-ac1728dd2f99" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix Given the Number of Non-Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3658fbf4-7125-51a3-8c67-6dac5efe7ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425383} {:answer/id #uuid "51f6e2e6-dc2b-5315-9b73-948670576a5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425385} {:answer/id #uuid "6da18174-0469-5de1-85a3-4a634932a54e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425389} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1d5e0a-36bb-506c-8445-a60981eb2cf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425395} {:answer/id #uuid "ef53b2d3-1206-58e8-a659-33784ef08b53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3658fbf4-7125-51a3-8c67-6dac5efe7ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425383} :answer-field/id #uuid "f829e1c6-fc4a-5157-b1d9-91868b24b67e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "85da25d6-54a2-55b2-b4ae-23095c708e42" :question/math-academy-id "q-79338" :question/problem "If $B$ is a $4\\times 6$ matrix that has $4$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(B))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $B.$\n\nSince we are told that $B$ has $4$ non-pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=4.\n$$"}]}
